from build_bank import *
add('At setup, where are the four starting Followers, Merchant, seven markers, unbuilt Trading Stations and coins placed; what do you receive personally, and who starts?', 'Each gets board, bag, Merchant, 10 stations, 5 coins, 7 markers and colored Farmer/Boatman/Craftsman/Trader. Starting Followers on Market, Merchant in Orléans, markers at first spaces of six Character Tracks and Development Track; stations/coins in front of player. Youngest starts.', ['pp.12–14; lines 20–56,104–111,120'],'Initial availability and board/personal placement')
add('How are Citizens, Technology, neutral Followers, Place Tile stacks, and map/remaining goods set up in a 4-player game?', '13 Citizens on marked main/Deed board spaces, remaining Citizen aside. Technology supply on board; neutral Followers sorted by profession in buildings. Places sorted I/II. Shuffle goods face down, put one face up per Road/Waterway goods space, sort leftovers face up to Goods Market.', ['pp.12–13; lines 25–44,59–73'],'Shared setup, market versus map destinations')
add('Specify the neutral Follower and random Goods removals and the empty map goods-space labels for both 3-player and 2-player setup. What happens to unused colored starting Followers?', '3 players remove 2 each Farmer/Boatman/Craftsman/Trader, 3 each Knight/Scholar/Monk, 6 random goods; leave 4 spaces empty. 2 players remove 4 each first four types, 6 each last three, 12 random goods; leave 3/4 spaces empty. Remove unused colors starting Followers.', ['p.13; lines 74–98'],'Player-count-dependent supply and map setup')
add('Before substitutions or Technology, list the required Followers for Farm House, Village, University, Castle and Monastery.', 'Farm House Boatman+Craftsman; Village Farmer+Boatman+Craftsman; University Farmer+Craftsman+Trader; Castle Farmer+Boatman+Trader; Monastery Scholar+Trader.', ['PDF p.12 player-board illustration (player-board-costs-p12.png); p.15 example lines176–177'],'Printed recruitment activation costs omitted from prose extraction')
add('Before substitutions or Technology, list the required Followers for Ship, Wagon and Guildhall.', 'Ship Farmer+Boatman+Knight; Wagon Farmer+Trader+Knight; Guildhall Farmer+Craftsman+Knight.', ['PDF p.12 player-board illustration (player-board-costs-p12.png)'],'Printed travel and construction activation costs')
add('Before substitutions or Technology, what Followers activate Scriptorium, and what professions are allowed in Town Hall?', 'Scriptorium Knight+Scholar. Town Hall one or two neutral Followers of any profession, but no colored starting Followers; Deed destinations must match exact depicted professions.', ['PDF p.12 player-board illustration; p.18 lines279–296'],'Printed Development activation and generic Town Hall slots')
add('In Phase 3 your allowance is six. May you decline two draws to recover two Followers assigned to actions? Where do they go, and may you instead move them directly between Action Spaces?', 'Yes: draw four and recover two assigned Followers into Market (subject to space). One recovery per declined draw in Phase3; cannot transfer directly between Action Spaces.', ['p.21; lines392–395; p.14 lines135–139'],'Recovery timing and direct-transfer prohibition')
add('May you look into your Followers Bag during play to check its contents? What must you do afterward?', 'May inspect bag at any time for number/types, then shuffle so draws cannot be chosen deliberately.', ['p.21; lines384–386'],'Private bag inspection and randomized draws')
add('List the seven round phases in order. How does Start Player change, and how is order handled if simultaneous Planning or payments require a sequence? Where do paid and received coins go?', 'Hour Glass, Census, Followers, Planning, Actions, Event, Start Player. Token to player left. Start planning simultaneously; announce completion; if needed clockwise from Start Player; payments same order. Coins paid to/received from common supply.', ['pp.14–15; lines121–175; p.21 lines396–401'],'Phase sequence, simultaneous planning and payment priority')
add('The 18th Hour Glass tile has just been revealed. Do you score immediately, or what part of play remains?', 'Complete that entire round, including actions and event; then final Trading Station Citizen award and scoring.', ['p.14 lines123–125; p.19 lines317–320'],'Final-round end trigger and remaining phases')
add('One player has more Farmer tiles in their bag, but a different player is uniquely ahead on the Farmers Track. Who gains the Census coin?', 'Use Farmers Track marker position, not physical tiles currently owned/in bag. Unique track leader gains 1 coin.', ['p.14 lines129–133'],'Track state versus current Follower ownership')
add('How much does Income pay and what current value determines it?', 'Coins equal to current Development Status, not raw position counted as Development Points.', ['p.20 lines346–347; p.19 lines311–316'],'Income event value basis')
add('You have eight goods at Taxes. How much must you pay, do goods types change that calculation, and what happens if you lack the coins?', 'Pay 2 coins, one per complete group of three goods regardless of type; shortage triggers torture for missing coins.', ['p.20 lines352–354'],'Taxes complete-group rounding and payment failure')
add('At Trading Day you have four built stations and six unbuilt in reserve. How much do you receive?', '4 coins, one per built Trading Station; unbuilt stations do not count.', ['p.20 lines355–356'],'Trading Day built-only income')
add('For each of Hayrick, Cheese Factory, Winery, Wool Manufacturer and Tailor Shop, give the printed activation cost, produced good, its source, and whether you may use it when that good is unavailable there.', 'Hayrick Farmer→grain; Cheese Factory two Farmers→cheese; Winery Farmer+Trader→wine; Wool Manufacturer Boatman+Trader→wool; Tailor Shop Scholar+Trader→brocade. Each takes one from Goods Market, and cannot be used if that type absent.', ['PDF p.22 tile illustrations; lines408–410'],'Five base production Places, costs and local exhaustion')
add('Give the printed activation cost and reward for Shipping Line, Brewery, Windmill and Library.', 'Shipping Line Boatman:1 Development Point. Brewery Monk:2 coins. Windmill two Craftsmen:2 coins plus1 Development Point. Library Knight+Scholar:2 Development Points.', ['PDF p.22 tile illustrations; lines411–433'],'Distinct printed base development/coin Place effects')
add('Which Follower can activate Pharmacy, what is the legal coin-spending range, and how far does it advance you if you pay two? May you use its effect for zero or four coins?', 'Any one Character can activate. Spend1–3 coins for equal Development spaces; two coins moves2. Cannot spend zero or four.', ['p.22 Pharmacy illustration; lines434–442'],'Flexible activation with bounded voluntary payment')
add('Give the printed activation cost and coin reward for Cellar, Office and Hospital. What quantity sets each variable payout?', 'Cellar Monk+Scholar:4 coins. Office two Scholars:1 coin per built station. Hospital Boatman+Scholar:coins equal current Development Status.', ['PDF pp.22–23 tile illustrations; lines443–451,514–522'],'Fixed versus built-station and Development-Status Place income')
add('What activates Horse Wagon, what route and distance does it travel, and what does it collect?', 'Trader+Knight. Merchant moves along one Road to adjacent town and collects one good if available.', ['PDF p.23 Horse Wagon illustration; lines531–539'],'Alternative road action with its distinct cost')
add('What activates Laboratory and what does it give? Could your first ever Technology be placed on Laboratory itself, and could a later one be placed there if no Technology is already on it?', 'Scholar+Craftsman; gives Technology under usual constraints. First must replace Farmer, which Laboratory lacks, so first cannot go there. Later can replace Scholar or Craftsman there if no existing Technology (not Monk; max one per Place).', ['PDF p.23 Laboratory illustration; lines480–486; p.16 lines209–218'],'Laboratory acquisition and first-tile placement interaction')
add('What activates Bathhouse? Describe its normal draw-three procedure, when and where the chosen tiles go, the forbidden destination, and where all other involved Followers go.', 'Farmer activates. Draw3 bag Followers, choose2, immediately place on matching Action Spaces; none on Bathhouse. Third drawn and activating Farmer return to bag.', ['PDF p.23 Bathhouse illustration; lines545–549'],'Original-edition Bathhouse immediate placement and destinations')
add('Bathhouse draws three Followers, but only one can legally be placed on any allowed Action Space. What may you place and where do the others and the activating Follower go? What if none can be placed?', 'Place the one immediately; return other two and activating Follower to bag. If none fit, place none and return all three plus activating Follower. Never place Bathhouse draws on Bathhouse.', ['p.23 lines545–549'],'Bathhouse insufficient-placement branch')
add('During the Action Phase, Bathhouse immediately supplies the last needed Follower to another Place. Must that newly activated Place wait for next round, or may you execute it on a later action turn this round if you have not passed?', 'May execute on a later own action turn this round: Bathhouse places immediately, and full activation allows action during current/future Action Phase; no extra Planning Phase required. Cannot act after passing.', ['p.23 lines545–549; p.15 lines154–170'],'Bathhouse changes activation during Actions rather than Planning')
add('What activates Sacristy, when is its protection used, which events can it protect against, and where does its Monk go?', 'A Monk activates. During Event Phase return Monk to bag instead of suffering current negative event such as Harvest, Taxes or Plague.', ['PDF p.23 Sacristy illustration; lines464–470'],'Sacristy event-phase consumption/protection')
add('Does an activated Sacristy let you recruit a Monk during a Pilgrimage round? Explain the timing.', 'No. Pilgrimage forbids Monk recruitment in Phase5 Actions. Sacristy substitutes for negative effects during Phase6 Event and cannot cancel that earlier prohibition.', ['p.20 lines343–345; p.23 lines464–470'],'Sacristy protection timing versus exceptional Pilgrimage timing')
add('What does Herb Garden allow Boatmen to replace, and does it permit replacing Knights, Scholars or Monks?', 'Ongoing ability, no activation: Boatmen replace Craftsmen, Traders and Farmers only. Does not permit Boatmen to replace Knights, Scholars or Monks.', ['PDF p.23 Herb Garden tile; lines506–513'],'Herb Garden exact substitution set')
add('What does School allow Scholars to replace, does School require activation, and may a Scholar replace a required Monk?', 'Ongoing no-activation ability: Scholars may replace other Character types except Monks. Cannot replace Monk.', ['PDF p.23 School tile; lines523–530'],'School ongoing substitution and Monk exception')
add('With Herb Garden or School, can a substituted Boatman or Scholar fill a differently depicted Beneficial Deed space? Does using Gunpowder Tower instead of Town Hall change that?', 'No: Deeds always require exact depicted types regardless of substitution abilities or route through Town Hall/Tower.', ['p.18 lines290–293; p.23 lines498–513,523–530'],'Global exact-type exception overrides acquired substitution/routing abilities')
add('Describe Gunpowder Tower: how much capacity it adds, when Followers enter it, the two ways to use them, whether two can go to Deeds in one action, and whether colored starting Followers can be sent.', 'Adds2 Market spaces; put1/2 drawn Followers there in Phase3. In Planning move one/both onto Action Spaces, or during Actions send one/both directly to matching Deed spaces in a single action. Cannot send colored starting Followers to Deeds.', ['p.23 lines498–505'],'Tower capacity, dual timing and direct Deed action')
add('In a 3-player Census there is one unique leader and two players tied furthest behind. Who gains and who pays?', 'Unique leader gains1 coin. Neither tied-last player pays.', ['p.14 lines129–131'],'Separate tied-minimum Census outcome not in Q01 scenario')
